WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.310
All of us are at least 20 years old!

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.750
Th-that's not a burglar is it?!

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.220
Makoto-san?

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.890
What are you doing?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.890
Michiru...

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.640
I mean... Michiru-senpai!

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.390
Y-yeah?

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.060
As a working adult, please tell me
how I'm supposed to get through this job hunt!

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.020
Whaaaaaaa-?!

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.500
I don't even know what I want to do.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.250
How am I gonna get through this?

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.000
<i>She's trying to binge eat her stress away.</i>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.050
Why don't you try visiting
with some alumni from your school?

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:37.340
Huh? Alumni?

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:40.390
So you can ask them all about
how they got where they are.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.180
You could invite some other classmates
and have everyone go out for drinks together.

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.180
That sounds perfect!

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.730
But what if it doesn't go well...?

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:50.270
Wh-what exactly are you worried about?

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:53.690
I've gotta figure out
what proper manners towards them are...

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.690
And how I'm even supposed to address them...

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.280
This girl doesn't know anything, huh?

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.910
I'll make sure HR hears this.

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:03.410
You really don't have to be so worried.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.740
But I don't want to be rude or anything.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.160
I want to at least know the basic rules and stuff...

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.670
Well in that case, let's ask everyone!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.590
"Everyone"?

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.170
Huh? You want to meet
with your school alumni over drinks?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:23.140
I need you to teach me the proper manners
for engaging with people who are older than me.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:26.100
Well I mean, they're still
pretty much around your age, right?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.560
You really don't have to worry that much.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:32.400
But don't you have to make sure you never have the wrong beer to foam ratio when you pour for them?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.730
No, of course not!

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.900
Did someone say "beer"?

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:37.570
Huh?

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:41.990
When you're pouring a bottle of beer,
make sure you have the label facing up.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.570
W-wait really?

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:47.450
Sometimes you actually come in handy, huh?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:50.200
Hey now, I'm a full-time working adult too, you know!

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.580
Well then, why don't we have some practice drinks?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.330
Huh?

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:58.340
We'll practice sharing some drinks
with people who are your senior.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.340
Yes! Let's do exactly that!

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:06.600
<i>And so we ended up holding the so-called
"Stella House Workforce Social."</i>

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.930
Okay then, time to do some shopping!

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.100
Now then...

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.320
If you want to get acquainted with
the businessman's beer of choice this would be it!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.360
Asahi Super Dry!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.780
Whoa!

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.700
This is the number one top selling beer in Japan!

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:26.490
Let's use that for our little social, then.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:33.000
Super Dry was introduced in 1987
as Japan's first dry beer.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.960
Back then heavy, bitter beers were the norm,

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.500
but this crisp refreshing beer brought about a revolution!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.380
Does Makoto even like beer?

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.410
I don't think she hates it or anything,

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:46.760
but I guess she's not usually a beer-drinker.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:52.810
Me, though, I almost lose it when I see them
bring out a bunch of bottles at the start!

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.560
They don't last very long, do they?

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:59.440
Wanna get some edamame?

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:01.610
How about some cheese puffs, too?

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:01.720
Oh! Good call~
How about some cheese puffs, too?

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:02.240
Oh! Good call~

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.530
<i>Do they even remember why we're here...?</i>

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:07.820
<i>I never thought I'd feel so nervous at home...</i>

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.030
Makoto-san.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.040
Chief Kiriyama and Chairwoman Midorikawa
are waiting!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.830
It's already time, so please get to your seat.

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:21.280
Company social rule number one: Never be late!

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.550
Makoto-san, that's where the higher ups sit!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.590
Huh?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:25.680
Rule number two:
Huh?

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.010
Rule number two:

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.260
The seat furthest away, is for the head
and the closer ones are for subordinates.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:35.810
Remember that junior employees should sit near the door, so they can order food and drinks easily!

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:39.060
So these are the sorts of things
you need to watch out for, huh...?

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.820
<i>Getting to play the senpai role is awesome!</i>

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.070
Well hello there, Makoto-kun.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.030
What an unbecoming chief...

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.280
Watch your language!

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.700
I'm big and important you know!

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.910
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.330
We were awaiting your arrival, Chairwoman Midorikawa!

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.670
Whoa, Kae, tone it down!

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:02.420
<i>She means business!</i>

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.630
This is just an act, okay?!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.510
Makoto-san. Please pour a drink for our chief.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:09.590
Y-yes, ma'am!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:16.890
Company social rule number three:
Don't rest the bottle on top of the glass!

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:21.480
Company social rule number four:
Always hold the bottle with both hands!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:35.080
Makoto poured a beer just for me!

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.370
You need to stay in character!
Makoto poured a beer just for me!

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.660
You need to stay in character!

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.580
Allow me to pour a glass for Makoto-kun, then.

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.000
Oh! Thank you!

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.960
Company social rule number five:

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.010
Hold one hand under your glass
when someone is pouring for you!

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.890
Why are there so many different rules just for drinking?

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:59.940
D-don't worry about them too much!

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:04.110
Now that everyone has a drink in hand...

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.610
Cheers!

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.110
I'd say you like it, Makoto-kun!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.410
I'm just tired out from my after school activities and stuff!

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.660
That stress is just the thing, to spice up a good beer!

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.620
So, how does it taste?

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.830
It really hits you in the back of the throat...

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:25.340
First it hits you!

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.380
Then you get that sweet relief
that makes it taste all the better!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.760
That taste earns it the name "Dry"!

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:34.140
You can enjoy washing it down just as is...

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.430
But getting it nice and frosty,
before gulping it down is also great!

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:44.650
You can drink Super Dry Extra Cold
at sub-zero temperatures at some bars, you know!

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.400
That's always a joy to find on a menu!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.530
Now then, Makoto-kun...

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.780
is there anything you would like to ask
working adults like ourselves?

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:53.570
Wha-?

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.030
Oh yes.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:59.410
If you're going to meet with some alumni,
you'll want to have questions ready beforehand.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.790
So, do you, Makoto-kun?

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.300
Well, I guess what I want to know most,

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.800
is why you chose the job you did... Maybe...

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.130
Mhmm. Mhmm.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:17.810
If there's any good way to find work that suits you,
I'd like to know what it is.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.310
Well you see...

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.060
You'll never know, until you actually try it out!

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.060
That doesn't answer anything...

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.650
But you'll just have to accept that.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:34.070
The way you'll see things before starting
and afterwards, will hardly be the same at all.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.740
Don't go making faces, now.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:40.240
We've got plenty to go with that beer.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:43.080
Wow! I'll take some salmon, then!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:47.590
Mmm! So fatty, sweet, and delish!

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:51.010
Those fish oils, the soy sauce,
and now some Super Dry...

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:57.850
The beer is so crisp, that it really brings out
the flavor in the fish!

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.720
Well, of course it does...

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.350
That beer right there!

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:07.520
The whole concept behind its creation,
was to make a beer that goes well with sashimi!

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.610
And then there's this label! Metallic silver!

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.360
Back when it was first made,

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:15.490
some people in the company complained it didn't look very beer-like.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.780
But it really suits the idea of a dry beer
and just looks pretty cool anyway!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.990
It's the color of the can itself.

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:27.120
Nowadays it's basically the most
recognizable beer can design around.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.880
That's because it held on
to its core concept without faltering!

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.960
<i>Sticking to its core concept...</i>

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.860
<i>I read in a book that sticking to core points,
can help in a job search, too...</i>

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.310
<i>But what are my core points?</i>

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.020
Do you like your job now?

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.770
If I didn't, I wouldn't make it through the day...

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.520
Picking out outfits that suit a customer,

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.820
giving out fashion advice,

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.030
I love that sort of stuff.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:59.870
You used to even make
handmade outfits for my dolls, huh?

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:03.080
Whoa! Blast from the past, much?!

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.750
I was just thinking how you haven't changed one bit.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:10.920
Okay! I think I feel a bit better about all this now!

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:12.630
Michiru...

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:17.550
Kae-san too, thanks for helping me out with all this.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.340
Keep those spirits up, Makoto-chan.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:23.850
And well, all that advice and stuff, Sis...

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:29.940
It really helped.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.570
Nao-san, cut it out!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:34.690
S-stop it!

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:38.450
Jeez! I'm trying to be grateful here
so you could at least listen!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:43.990
<i>Company social rule number six:
Be careful not to get drunk!</i>

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:53.540
<i>I learned all the basic rules,
so I should be able to do this!</i>

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.470
Kiriyama-san you're great at pouring!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.470
Th-thank you!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.510
Oh, would you like some more beer?

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.100
Oh, sure! How nice of you!

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.310
<i>Alright!</i>

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.190
If you ever have any questions, just text me.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.980
Thank you!

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:15.120
See you, then!

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.320
<i>They were so nice.</i>

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.200
<i>What was I even afraid of?</i>

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:26.200
<i>This job search... I think it might actually be fun!</i>

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.000
That's great to hear!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.080
Sounds like our little practice was worth it.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.250
Way to go, Makoto-san!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:35.000
I owe you all for that.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.010
So what all did they talk about?

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:41.010
Huh?

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.510
Shoot!

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:48.310
I was so worried about the drinks and stuff,
that I don't even remember a word they said!

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:55.480
<i>Makoto-san may have taken her first step towards finding herself a job, or maybe not!</i>
